From b6a4cd9916f4a4fbf9e0d838ec798fd4d698329b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GitHub Copilot <copilot@github.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Apr 2026 14:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: agent terminal "Run in Terminal" throws ENOPRO in
 code-server web browser

Three-part fix for the ENOPRO error when using the agent host terminal
integration (e.g. Copilot's "Run in Terminal") in code-server.

Root cause chain:
1. AgentHostPty.start() serialised the cwd URI via .toString() →
   "file:///home/coder/dev/project" was sent to the agent host.
2. agentHostTerminalManager passed that URI string verbatim to node-pty
   as the working directory (node-pty expects a plain filesystem path).
3. In the browser renderer getCwdResource() called
   pathService.fileURI(cwd) which again produces file:// URIs, then
   fileService.exists(file://...) threw ENOPRO because the browser
   renderer has no DiskFileSystemProvider for file://.

Fixes:
1. agentHostPty.ts: send cwd.fsPath instead of cwd.toString()
2. agentHostTerminalManager.ts: defensive URI-string → path conversion;
   update ICreateTerminalParams.cwd type from URI to string
3. terminalInstance.ts getCwdResource(): build vscode-remote:// URI in
   remote contexts; add try/catch around fileService.exists()
